What is the Yomi Denzel Foundation?

Yomi's journey began as a broke student. A child of an African immigrant and Swiss mum. He learnt early from his very hardworking parents who could not meet his financial need despite their hardwork and effort.

His knowledge of his Dad’s ambition not to be poor but frustrated by limited opportunity in Africa planted the seed of maximizing opportunity that came his way. Yomi therefore dedicated himself to mastering digital skills and entrepreneurship.

Today, his passion to see young people financially independent, in Nigeria, led him to begin the Yomi Denzel Foundation.

At the Yomi Denzel Foundation (YDF), we believe in the transformative power of education and resilience. Our mission is to empower Nigerian youths with the digital skills and mindset needed to achieve financial independence.

We are committed to providing free, high-quality training in digital skills, programming languages and e-commerce. We believe that by equipping young Nigerians with these essential skills, we can help them secure better job opportunities locally and globally and attain financial freedom.

We create training opportunities computer languages such as Python, Machine Learning and Data Science and Blockchain . The goal is to equip young school leavers with essential skills to earn income even while studying.

Since inception, we have graduated two sets of young school leavers and presently equipping the third set of young Nigerians.

Our graduates have been securing internships with top Fin tech firms online and offline. They have won Hackathon laurels and prizes, started their own businesses and earning income with the skills acquired through the Foundation. Their success stories are a testament to the power of education and determination.

Whether you're looking to gain new skills, start a business, or simply improve your personal development, YDF is here to support you.

Follow our page for updates on upcoming programs, success stories, and tips on achieving your goals.

